{
  "name": "arkworks-algebra",
  "description": "A comprehensive Rust-based suite of high-performance algebraic primitives optimized for the construction and verification of zero-knowledge succinct non-interactive arguments (zkSNARKs). It provides strictly-typed abstractions for finite fields, elliptic curve groups, and polynomial arithmetic, leveraging handwritten assembly (ADX/BMI2) for low-level arithmetic acceleration on x86_64 architectures. The codebase implements a broad spectrum of pairing-friendly curves, R1CS-compatible arithmetic circuits, and efficient point compression algorithms required for scalable decentralized computation.",
